vo: add a shared subtitle/OSD render-ahead pipeline

vo_mediacodec renders subtitles on a thread of its own, ahead of the video
that shows them: a request per frame as soon as the frame is known, a
latest-wins mailbox, a bounded result FIFO, a pre-render of the frame the
cadence predicts next, and while the OSD is static, of the next subtitle
event's first frame. Nothing in that pipeline is specific to MediaCodec, and
vo_avfoundation needs the same thing instead of a second implementation.

Add it as video/out/osd_ahead.[ch]. The code is vo_mediacodec's render
stage moved as is; what was specific to that VO is now supplied by the VO:
the canvas size and OSD geometry (callbacks, latched under the lock where
the geometry used to be copied), the render thread's priority, and the
presentation itself. The next patch switches vo_mediacodec to it.

scripts/test_mediacodec_osd.sh compiles the scheduler core and the request
dispatcher from this file.

